{
  "paraId": "51AF64F4",
  "style": "",
  "text": "The optimal dose of antiangiogenic agents helps improve TIME 27. Anlotinib (3 mg/kg) boosts the antitumor efficacy of radioimmunotherapy 28. , but the dose-dependence of its effect on TIME is unexplored. Here, anlotinib (3 mg/kg) plus radiation did not increase the percentage of CD8+ T cells versus IR alone (Supplementary Fig. 8), whereas anlotinib (1.5 mg/kg) reportedly breaks through the immunosuppressive barrier to potentiate TIME 29. Consistently, low-dose (1.5 mg/kg) anlotinib plus IR normalized blood vessels (Supplementary Fig. 9), and low-dose (1.5 mg/kg) anlotinib was therefore used in subsequent experiments. Nevertheless, the optimal anlotinib dose remains controversial and warrants further study."
}

