  "text": "Reportedly, poorly immunogenic tumors have little response to immunotherapy. LLC is a highly aggressive and poorly immunogenic tumor model that is barely responsive to antitumor immunotherapy 25. LLC-OVA, more immunogenic than LLC, remains resistant to immunotherapy 26. In the current study, only tumor growth was delayed and exhausted T cells decreased in the radioimmunotherapy group compared to IR alone, whereas CD8+ T cell proliferation and immune memory activation were not increased. Moreover, the decrease in Foxp3 expression was not observed in the radioimmunotherapy group compared to IR alone (Supplementary Fig. 7). These findings indicated that radioimmunotherapy could not sufficiently activate antitumor immunity. Conversely, triple therapy appeared to reduce CD8+ T cell exhaustion and tumor-infiltrating Tregs, and was associated with enhanced proliferation, activation, and immune memory of CD8+ T cells. Taken together, these findings suggest that triple therapy may have produced the most favorable changes in the TIME among the regimens tested, although this interpretation is limited by the readouts examined and warrants further validation."
